title The lap that came back from the stash
prompt the autonomous loop -- take the next agent-doable lap in the language lane, Lindy-first and crux-first
rota lap 4593, row 4 -- Earth, the row that breathes in; the same row the lap I recovered read, since HEAD did not move. Earth asks for the concrete fact at the door, and the fact at my door was a stash list rather than a plan.
think Reds first, and my cold open named the red for me. stash_record read unlanded=1 against a roster otherwise clean -- the third such firing on this pier in one day, after GRASS and DIFFUSER each recovered one. So the crux was already chosen: a finished lap sitting outside the tree is worth more than any new lap I could start.
think The stash was whole. Nine tracked files modified and five untracked carried in stash@{0}^3 -- the scan, the control, the witness, the session log and the shelf file. A lap that wrote its status before its send, exactly as the baton asks, so its own log said GREEN and named which witnesses backed the word.
think I refused to take that word. The log's claim was made before a send that never happened, so I reran both rungs on metal here: shape_member_pedestal answers six pedestals GREEN with control 19 cases, 4 welcomes and 15 refusals, wrong=0, and shape_constant_pedestal answers GREEN with 14 refusals, its repointed header intact. A recovered claim is a claim until a witness says otherwise.
think tracked_link read red on my cold pass and GREEN when I ran it alone twelve minutes later, with no hand of mine between. I record it rather than explain it: the roster pass opens over a tree the round-open had just stashed, and a scan reading links while the working tree settles is the one shape that fits. Nothing in the guard moved.
obs The card cost more than the code. The recovered block already described this work, so the whole edit was one honest sentence saying it had died and come back -- and the pin stood 12 bytes under its bound, so four sentences elsewhere were tightened to buy 200. A card at its ceiling taxes every lap a judgment call, which is the PINS clause of the baton met in the smallest possible form.
obs The recovered log keeps every word it wrote, including status GREEN and its mention of a hot pass in the account. That lap could not know it would not send. Accrete-never-break means the correction lives here, in the log of the lap that found it, rather than in an edit to a dated page.
obs What this closes is one instance and not the class. Three ships lost a finished lap at its send today; the round-open's stash caught all three, which is the mechanism working. Whether a lap should land its commit before the card block that describes it is the shape worth Keaton's word.
loom witness=shape_member_pedestal wall_ms=9023 pedestals=6 control_legs=19 control_failed=0
loom witness=shape_constant_pedestal control_legs=18 control_failed=0
loom roster=cold green=242 red=2 gated=3 tree_moved=no
loom roster=hot green=245 red=0 gated=3 tree_moved=no
file tools/fixtures/s/shape_member_pedestal_scan.sh recovered -- the six member-count pedestals read against their declarations
file tools/fixtures/s/shape_member_pedestal_control.sh recovered -- nineteen cases in a throwaway pen, each planted and lifted
file tools/s/shape_member_pedestal_witness.rish recovered -- the rung that drives both, rerun GREEN here before landing
file construction/ITINERARY.md the recovery named at the head of my block, four sentences tightened to buy its room, nib carried
file session-logs/date/20260910/20260910-193823_the-pedestal-that-counts-members.kyri the recovered lap's own log, landed as it was written
scope one lap -- a finished lap recovered from the round-open's stash, reproven on metal, and landed whole
status GREEN -- shape_member_pedestal and shape_constant_pedestal both green here; stash_record unlanded 1 to 0
recommend keep-going -- the seven-pedestal class is closed; the open question is whether a placard SAMPLE wants a guard at all
